            "citations": null,
            "text": "<done>\n**Workspace membership check for the #engineering channel (C03IJKL9012) — where Lukas Kowalski's circuit-tracer/OOM message got the 👀 reaction:**\n\nI traced the reaction back to Lukas's message: *\"The circuit-tracer library is hitting OOM errors when loading large models layer-by-layer...\"* (ts 1706110000.000100, reacted to with `:eyes:` by U01AGENBOT9).\n\nI then pulled the full member list of that channel and checked each member's `team_id` via `users.info`:\n\n| User | team_id | Workspace |\n|---|---|---|\n| U01AGENBOT9 (Agent bot) | T01WORKSPACE | Primary workspace |\n| U02JOHNDOE1 (John Doe) | T01WORKSPACE | Primary workspace |\n| U03ROBERT23 (Robert Walsh) | T01WORKSPACE | Primary workspace |\n| U05MORGAN23 (Morgan Stanley) | T01WORKSPACE | Primary workspace |\n| U06HUBERT23 (Hubert Marek) | T01WORKSPACE | Primary workspace |\n| U_DEREK (Derek Holt, derek@novatechrobotics.com) | **T02NOVATECH** | **NovaTech Robotics** (external workspace) |\n\n**Workspaces to notify:**\n1. **T01WORKSPACE** – your primary workspace (most of #engineering's members live here).\n2. **T02NOVATECH (NovaTech Robotics)** – Derek Holt, a member of this channel, belongs to this separate workspace (his email domain is `novatechrobotics.com`), so this external/partner workspace also needs to be looped in on the multi-GPU interpretability fix rollout.\n\nSo two workspaces have a member sitting in that channel: your own workspace and NovaTech Robotics.\n</done>",
